          "tag": "Saying Fits",
          "text": "Harold’s friends were surprised when he revealed that he had left his wallet at home and asked that someone lend him money. But he had done the same thing many times before. As Halliard said, “The force of selfishness is as inevitable and as calculable as the force of gravitation. ”"
        },
        {
          "is_correct": false,
          "letter": "C",
          "tag": "Saying Fits",
          "text": "The best model of vacuum cleaner was the most expensive on the market, but it would have made Roger unhappy to purchase it. For although he never wanted anything but the best, he was also quite frugal, and would never have forgiven himself for spending the money. As the saying goes, “A penny saved is a penny earned.”"
        },
        {
          "is_correct": false,
          "letter": "D",
          "tag": "Saying Fits",
          "text": "Sharon loved cats, but her husband was allergic to them. Still, he was occasionally willing to accompany her to cat shows. As the saying goes, “Shared lives mean shared loves. ”"
        },
        {
          "is_correct": true,
          "letter": "E",
          "tag": "Correct",
