      ],
      "explanation_id": "729c3586-c0e3-467a-bf5b-e4777357a59f",
      "notes": [
        {
          "body": "Fatima knows enough mathematics to see how much will stay unsolved. That's the saying in action: you need to know a lot before you see how little you know. The story illustrates it, so the phrase is used properly.",
          "id": "d00c8c91-11f8-4fe2-a9b4-d49d99046cb6",
          "letter": "A",
          "md5": "cf4951c56a56f79b014dc261c4d557e9"
        },
        {
          "body": "Harold has done the same thing many times before. That's selfishness as predictable as gravity, so the quote matches the story. The friends' surprise doesn't change that Harold's behavior was calculable.",
          "id": "3b5bc32b-2e4d-446c-bb7d-559f738d834e",
          "letter": "B",
          "md5": "ddf80215e89609c3b32f29c1c258cb5f"
        },
        {
          "body": "Roger won't buy the expensive vacuum because Roger is frugal and would never forgive the spending. \"A penny saved is a penny earned\" is the frugal person's motto, so the story illustrates it and the phrase is used properly.",
          "id": "c8e1214f-182c-45d9-970c-7cd03c222039",
          "letter": "C",
          "md5": "3365c05b9856d9fe4af7391bc3ea1df2"
        },
        {
          "body": "Sharon loves cats, and Sharon's husband, despite the allergy, still sometimes comes along to cat shows. Sharing a life with Sharon means sharing what Sharon loves, at least a little. The story illustrates the saying.",
          "id": "77288382-68a7-4a80-bc42-a34e310b261c",
          "letter": "D",
          "md5": "6a9cf339f3c263281f72fca4870b3762"
        },
        {
          "body": "Raoul's trip ended with a broken leg and two weeks in the hospital. That didn't end well, so \"All's well that ends well\" has no illustration here. The story is an apparent counterexample, and putting \"as the saying goes\" after it is the misuse the principle describes.",
          "id": "7bdb2eef-4417-4768-bb53-a07a7e234a49",
