        },
        {
          "body": "Look at how Raoul's story actually ends: a broken leg and two weeks in the hospital. That is the opposite of \"all's well that ends well.\" The trip did not end well at all.\n\nThe principle says \"as the saying goes\" should follow a story that illustrates the saying. Here the story is the reverse — a counterexample. Using \"as the saying goes\" to introduce a saying that the story contradicts is exactly the inappropriate usage the principle warns about.",
          "id": "a714c64b-aa03-4875-8df3-8ccf0f0846bd",
          "letter": "E",
          "md5": "eda9f61178595838c2b092daea89afa8"
        }
      ],
