      "explanation_id": "8041685f-9e1b-41aa-8609-2626f0307c39",
      "notes": [
        {
          "body": "This principle is about who should regulate (international agreements). The actual debate is whether Figoria should regulate at all, given that wildlife \"might not\" be affected. The principle does not pick a winner between the two sides.",
          "id": "4877dcf3-2c27-4f07-a143-b801e44555c6",
          "letter": "A",
          "md5": "b90b8ed91f1eb64ff3d437e034b9a5b8"
        },
        {
          "body": "This principle says preserving wildlife matters more than meeting current economic needs. That is exactly the opposite of what the Development Commission is arguing — they are saying growth is necessary and the wildlife impact is uncertain. This principle would crush their position, not strengthen it.",
          "id": "1ffbeba8-55ee-4cc6-8ca8-7770fbc9a738",
          "letter": "B",
          "md5": "a4f68a40609a8548a5ab4c035da80970"
        },
        {
          "body": "This is the principle the Development Commission needs. It says regulation only kicks in once a population has actually been reduced by commercial development.\n\nApply that to Figoria: no reduction has happened yet (Figoria has conserved), and the planned development \"might not\" affect wildlife. Under this rule, regulation is not yet justified — so the Development Commission's \"let us develop\" position wins.\n\nThe Wildlife Commission's precautionary, regulate-up-front stance directly conflicts with this principle, which is the contrast the question is looking for.",
          "id": "8b898f14-e417-4d98-ba34-2e2c0ba7d752",
          "letter": "C",
          "md5": "62c46f63c40c06ed802c8bc2df377f3a"
        },
        {
          "body": "Read this carefully — it actually undercuts the Development Commission. They wanted special treatment *because* Figoria has not yet harmed wetlands like other nations have. This principle says you cannot give that kind of credit; everyone must just prevent further damage. That favors immediate regulation, which is the Wildlife Commission's position.",
          "id": "85e31dce-aa30-42d8-839b-57f14f6e4002",
          "letter": "D",
          "md5": "e5255a158efea09247bd90089b3e6816"
        },
        {
          "body": "This principle treats further depletion as imprudent — full stop. The Development Commission wants to be allowed to deplete (develop) some wetlands. So this principle opposes their position rather than supporting it.",
          "id": "267985ee-4b44-4df8-abc8-cd6b816c1ec2",
          "letter": "E",
          "md5": "a20d4057dd803cb5d72afaafc35fe93e"
        }
      ],
      "qid": "PT118-S3-Q8",
      "step_count": 3
    },
    {
      "choices": [
        {
          "is_correct": false,
          "letter": "A",
          "tag": "Too Strong",
          "text": "Regular afternoon exercise is one of the things required for adequate deep-sleep."
        },
        {
          "is_correct": false,
          "letter": "B",
          "tag": "Unsupported",
          "text": "Exercise in the morning is almost as likely to have as many beneficial effects on sleep as is exercise in the afternoon."
        },
        {
          "is_correct": false,
          "letter": "C",
          "tag": "Too Strong",
          "text": "The best way to get increased deep-sleep is to induce a slight increase in body temperature just before bedtime."
        },
        {
          "is_correct": false,
          "letter": "D",
          "tag": "Too Strong",
          "text": "No one in the control group experienced a rise in body temperature just before bedtime."
        },
        {
          "is_correct": true,
          "letter": "E",
          "tag": "Correct",
          "text": "Raising body temperature slightly by taking a warm bath just before bedtime will likely result in increased deep-sleep."
        }
      ],
      "explanation_id": "ba027d65-3993-417a-9d15-840243736e99",
      "notes": [
        {
          "body": "\"Required\" means no one gets adequate deep sleep without afternoon exercise. The study only shows that exercisers got more deep sleep than a group that exercised little or not at all. And the mechanism points the other way: if heat is the cause, other sources of heat could do the job without exercise.",
          "id": "9c0ce691-0918-4027-bfba-0f5ea6a58ebc",
          "letter": "A",
          "md5": "846e7f22375d99364f1dad7fe70abf34"
        },
        {
          "body": "The mechanism depends on body heat lasting until after bedtime. Morning exercise never comes up, and its heat could easily wear off long before night. Nothing lets us compare morning exercise with afternoon exercise.",
          "id": "1ebea67e-4423-4cf3-aa35-c5e3edd1e656",
          "letter": "B",
          "md5": "e44cadeee0ece7b08be2e5ba928b3265"
        },
        {
          "body": "\"The best way\" needs a comparison with every other way to get deep sleep. The researcher describes one thing that helps. That supports \"this works,\" not \"nothing works better.\"",
          "id": "db0dc54b-4fa7-444a-8f01-1804375a5c5d",
          "letter": "C",
          "md5": "3e5ff4f44ba54350d329f5c19b281e49"
        },
        {
          "body": "This is the most popular wrong answer. \"No one\" covers every person in the control group. They exercised little, but someone could have been warmed by a hot meal or a fever. The study reports group results, not every individual.",
          "id": "1a80dc2a-0dce-41ef-929f-7669bef1f561",
          "letter": "D",
          "md5": "5441fbb84a00f2efaf77fbd77dc310b1"
        },
        {
          "body": "The researcher says deeper sleep comes from \"this extra heat,\" a slight rise in body temperature that lasts past bedtime. A warm bath just before bed produces that same condition, so the mechanism predicts it should help too. Notice the move: when a stimulus names the mechanism behind a result, the supported answer often applies that mechanism to a new case. \"Will likely\" is as strong as the mechanism allows, and no stronger.",
          "id": "5eb2188f-1b6a-4a72-ada2-eb0666580b82",
          "letter": "E",
          "md5": "3bb22cd2b2a2a6d85036feacd712edc2"
        }
      ],
      "qid": "PT119-S2-Q12",
      "step_count": 3
    },
