      "notes": [
        {
          "body": "This question asks how much salt was in the diet. But the argument's real problem is whether the rats started out with high blood pressure to begin with. Knowing the exact dosage does not help us answer that — whether it was 5 times or 10 times normal salt, we still need the baseline.",
          "id": "8dc647fc-ddee-44e0-a3b1-2139124b6afc",
          "letter": "A",
          "md5": "ac9ff9e948ecf36f6132ca28f18cf306"
        },
        {
          "body": "The conclusion is just about whether salt is connected to high blood pressure. Whether high blood pressure then leads to other health problems is a separate question. It does not help us evaluate the salt-to-blood-pressure link.",
          "id": "f7499360-bf33-48bc-a212-76d546ffbffe",
