      "notes": [
        {
          "body": "This answer says the ad demonstrates something about repeat customers. The ad never mentions repeat customers — it talks only about pride producing winners. This describes a move that simply isn't in the ad.",
          "id": "3cc22189-5e3e-432a-8bdc-7ad3409d7ae6",
          "letter": "A",
          "md5": "31aefe1db0f93e8a8c1a95919c11cd67"
        },
        {
          "body": "This is exactly the move the ad is making. The ad sets up an analogy: pride leads to dominance for Austin Stables in their industry. Then it says Barr Motor has the same kind of pride. The implied conclusion is that Barr is superior to its competitors in cars, just like Austin is superior to its competitors in horses.\n\nThe whole argument is built on the analogy — and the conclusion is a superiority claim. That's exactly what (B) says.",
          "id": "41a95662-6a28-44e0-99d4-b4fe927dd8f7",
          "letter": "B",
          "md5": "40a03aaf45571f87b88bd9ac2bf1c4b3"
        },
        {
          "body": "This answer says the ad *proves* Barr has a tradition of pride. But the ad just states it (\"for generations we at Barr Motor Company have demonstrated similar pride\") — no evidence is offered to back this up. Asserting and proving are different moves, and the ad does the former, not the latter.",
          "id": "e4e08fba-b09b-402e-b22e-e4b01ca7df95",
          "letter": "C",
          "md5": "ac89741b6e9fa2a4cc57fe60f0d8c788"
        },
        {
          "body": "The ad heavily plays up pride as the driver of Austin Stables' success — that's the whole hook for the Barr analogy. Understating pride's role would undermine the ad's own argument. So this is the opposite of what the ad actually does.",
          "id": "664abcb5-a787-4c5f-ad96-6b0971d174b7",
          "letter": "D",
          "md5": "0612c7325febd9deeafadb345f7c3791"
        },
        {
          "body": "The ad treats both as having a tradition of pride — it doesn't rank them by age. There's no claim that Barr's tradition predates Austin's. The ad just says Barr has demonstrated \"similar pride\" for generations, with no comparison of timelines.",
          "id": "8dbf8585-a10a-4e3c-86af-09df612f2f2d",
          "letter": "E",
          "md5": "abf6b6c277473fb78085991483200963"
        }
