      "explanation_id": "4b99bd6c-1d08-49aa-b24c-9e673b861bd6",
      "notes": [
        {
          "body": "The hippocampus is just one location mentioned where theta waves occur — the argument is not pinning anything on it. The flaw is elsewhere: in the leap from \"creativity comes with theta waves\" to \"theta waves produce creativity.\" This answer attacks the wrong target.",
          "id": "69c8dc01-bd8e-4ef1-b822-05b42ba1b82f",
          "letter": "A",
          "md5": "01059d6c9696d4cd116c7195968fec60"
        },
        {
          "body": "This says the argument missed that music is not needed for creativity. But the argument's conclusion is that one *can* attain creativity by listening to music — not that music is the only path. Even if there are other paths, the conclusion can still be valid. So pointing this out is not a real objection to the argument.",
          "id": "cf6fccad-4257-4238-991d-835be172293e",
          "letter": "B",
          "md5": "bb26f772d7595ad107790979b076df61"
        },
        {
          "body": "This raises a question about music delivery methods. It does not actually undermine the argument — even if live music also raises theta waves, that does not make tape-recorded music ineffective. The argument's conclusion only requires tapes to work, and this objection does not show they do not.",
          "id": "682d86a2-8bc5-4e97-8b55-5fd4cd557fe2",
          "letter": "C",
          "md5": "bdb919884bf343784d95fc2e39eefc87"
        },
        {
          "body": "Here is the real flaw. The stimulus tells us creativity is accompanied by theta waves. That means: when creativity is happening, theta waves are up. It does *not* tell us the reverse — that whenever theta waves are up, creativity is happening.\n\nSo music can spike theta waves without spiking creativity. Maybe relaxation, daydreaming, or zoning out also raises theta waves. The argument needed the reverse direction (theta waves → creativity) and never proved it.\n\nThis answer pinpoints exactly that: the increase in theta waves may not always come with creativity.",
          "id": "47691c25-d3af-4242-a845-64320a9b63f8",
          "letter": "D",
          "md5": "80b09234b0cd5cc7a1f267d499cfe541"
        },
        {
          "body": "This faults the argument for not establishing what theta waves look like in non-creative people. But the argument never makes that claim. It is not a flaw to fail to support a claim you never made.",
          "id": "92d92519-4238-49c8-978a-220be9770f4d",
          "letter": "E",
          "md5": "6a7847752df3d06c140a3b16dd9e815c"
        }
      ],
